      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the first digit of the base $8$ representation of $473_{10}$, we need to convert $473_{10}$ to base $8$. We do this by repeatedly dividing the number by $8$ and keeping track of the remainders.\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r|l}\n473 & 8 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\nDividing $473$ by $8$, we get $59$ with a remainder of $1$. So, the least significant digit (rightmost) of the base $8$ representation is $1$.\n\nNext, we take the quotient $59$ and divide it by $8$:\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r|l}\n59 & 8 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\nDividing $59$ by $8$, we get $7$ with a remainder of $3$. So, the next digit in the base $8$ representation is $3$.\n\nNext, we take the quotient $7$ and divide it by $8$:\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r|l}\n7 & 8 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\nDividing $7$ by $8$, we get $0$ with a remainder of $7$. So, the next digit in the base $8$ representation is $7$.\n\nSince the quotient is now $0$, we stop the division process. Reading the remainders from bottom to top, the base $8$ representation of $473_{10}$ is $731_8$.\n\nThe first digit of the base $8$ representation is $7$. Therefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{7}\n\\]",
