      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the first digit of the base \\(8\\) representation of \\(473_{10}\\), we need to convert \\(473_{10}\\) to base \\(8\\). The first step is to determine the highest power of \\(8\\) that is less than or equal to \\(473\\).\n\nThe powers of \\(8\\) are:\n\\[8^0 = 1, \\quad 8^1 = 8, \\quad 8^2 = 64, \\quad 8^3 = 512, \\quad 8^4 = 4096.\\]\nSince \\(8^4 = 4096\\) is greater than \\(473\\), the highest power of \\(8\\) we need is \\(8^3 = 512\\).\n\nWe start by determining how many times \\(512\\) fits into \\(473\\):\n\\[473 \\div 512 \\approx 0.9216.\\]\nThe integer part of the division is \\(0\\), so \\(512\\) does not fit into \\(473\\). This means we need to use \\(8^2 = 64\\) instead.\n\nNext, we determine how many times \\(64\\) fits into \\(473\\):\n\\[473 \\div 64 \\approx 7.3844.\\]\nThe integer part of the division is \\(7\\), so we multiply \\(64\\) by \\(7\\) to get \\(448\\). We then subtract \\(448\\) from \\(473\\) to find the remainder:\n\\[473 - 448 = 25.\\]\nNow, we move to the next lower power of \\(8\\), which is \\(8^1 = 8\\). We determine how many times \\(8\\) fits into \\(25\\):\n\\[25 \\div 8 \\approx 3.125.\\]\nThe integer part of the division is \\(3\\), so we multiply \\(8\\) by \\(3\\) to get \\(24\\). We then subtract \\(24\\) from \\(25\\) to find the remainder:\n\\[25 - 24 = 1.\\]\nFinally, we use the next lower power of \\(8\\), which is \\(8^0 = 1\\). We determine how many times \\(1\\) fits into \\(1\\):\n\\[1 \\div 1 = 1.\\]\nThe remainder is \\(0\\), and we have used up all the digits.\n\nThus, the base \\(8\\) representation of \\(473_{10}\\) is \\(673_8\\). The first digit of this representation is \\(6\\).\n\nTherefore, the first digit of the base \\(8\\) representation of \\(473_{10}\\) is \\(\\boxed{6}\\).",
